  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Integrated WASH, NFIs, and Protection for the IDPs and Famine-affected Population in Sheikan, Dilling, and Alidia in Kordufan. Consortium</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe project aligns with the urgent needs of the protection, NFIs, and WASH sectors, focusing on life-saving assistance for the IDPs and vulnerable host communities in Greater Kordofan states. The project will be designed based on protection, NFIs, and WASH cluster and technical working group recommendations, and in close coordination with the HAC and line ministries in South, West, and North Kordofan states. Project activities will depend on findings from consultations between OCHA and the WASH, Protection, and NFI clusters, as discussed in the last meeting conducted by OCHA and SHF with implementing partners. Additionally, the design of this project directly aligns with SHF priorities in targeting the most critical localities in need.ltbrgtThis project will be implemented in consortium with Alsalam Organization for Rural Development (AORD) and CAFA. Currently, LMI and AORD are jointly implementing a WASH response project funded by SHF, aimed at increasing the resilience of crisis-affected IDPs, refugees, and host communities Alidia,&#xa0;Dilling &#xa0;Sheikanin Greater Kordofan (West, South, and North Kordofan states). While the project provides critical emergency WASH services, there remains a need for additional interventions to address gaps in the targeted communities, including&#xa0;Alidia&#xa0;locality in West Kordofan. These needs were identified through state-level cluster coordination, feedback from technical line ministries such as WES, MoH, and MoSW, and consultations with targeted communities in Dilling, Sheikan, and Adaia during regular coordination meetings conducted by IAS/LMI and local partners.lt/pgtltpgtthe activities are designed based on the conflict sensitivity measures to avoid doing harm to the targeted communities and maximize the impact of the proposed interventions, the planned activities were proposed based on community consultation and technical line ministries and selected the best fit lifesaving interventions in the targeted communities.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
